From ab10e9c3a74b72db85fe679a2330415956b6f2aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Sam (local build)" <sam@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:30:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] dde-emu v1b: fix false 'TX SM stuck' fault that dropped
 0x3D; first-fault record, stats v2

Car test 1: FAULT 1 latched in cycle 53 and 0x3D never reached the bus.
Root cause: tx_busy_since was set at the 0x26 load and only re-checked when
housekeeping ran right after the next loads (SM busy each time), so at the
0x3D alarm it looked 759 us busy (>200 us) and the fault path took the pins
and stopped the SMs before 0x3D went out.

- watchdog now uses a per-TX deadline (length + start offset) + 20 us margin;
  unexpected busy needs 200 us continuous busy
- echo matched per slot+cycle within 1 ms; own duplicate echo never foreign
- FAULT 3 only after >=8 consecutive misses over >=2 cycles while locked
- faults auto re-arm after 2 s quiet; 3rd fault latches until host clear
- precheck 2.5 -> 1.2 us (r is rechecked after the push); late reasons counted
- first-fault record + late reasons in 0xa4 stats (v2, 128 bytes; first 64 =
  v1 layout); console prints EMU FAULT ... once
- core scheduling/build code placed in RAM
